<!-- SLIDE 2 : Agenda / Overview -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>What is SQL?</h2>
  <div class="grid two">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Definition</h3>
      <p>SQL (Structured Query Language) is the standard language used to communicate with relational databases. It lets us create, manipulate, and query data stored in tables.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Main Categories</h3>
      <p><b style="color:#38bdf8">DDL</b> — Data Definition Language → defines the <b>structure</b> of database objects (tables, schemas).<br><br>
         <b style="color:#f472b6">DML</b> — Data Manipulation Language → works with the <b>data inside</b> those objects.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 3 : DDL vs DML -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DDL vs DML — Quick Comparison</h2>
  <div class="compare">
    <div class="ddl-box">
      <h3 style="color:#38bdf8">DDL (4 Commands)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>CREATE — make a new table/object</li>
        <li>ALTER — modify an existing table</li>
        <li>DROP — delete the table completely</li>
        <li>TRUNCATE — remove all rows, keep table</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="dml-box">
      <h3>DML (3 Commands)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>INSERT — add new rows of data</li>
        <li>UPDATE — change existing data</li>
        <li>DELETE — remove rows of data</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 4 : CREATE -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DDL Command 1 — CREATE</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">CREATE</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Creates a new database object such as a table, along with its columns, data types, and constraints. This is the very first step in defining the database structure.</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="kw">CREATE TABLE</span> employees (
    emp_id     <span class="kw">INT PRIMARY KEY</span>,
    first_name <span class="kw">VARCHAR</span>(50) <span class="kw">NOT NULL</span>,
    last_name  <span class="kw">VARCHAR</span>(50),
    salary     <span class="kw">DECIMAL</span>(10,2),
    hire_date  <span class="kw">DATE</span> <span class="kw">DEFAULT</span> <span class="kw">CURRENT_DATE</span>
);</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 5 : ALTER -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DDL Command 2 — ALTER</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">ALTER</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Modifies the structure of an existing table — you can add new columns, remove columns, or change a column's data type. The data inside the table is preserved.</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Add a new column</span>
<span class="kw">ALTER TABLE</span> employees <span class="kw">ADD</span> email <span class="kw">VARCHAR</span>(100);

<span class="cm">-- Modify a column's data type</span>
<span class="kw">ALTER TABLE</span> employees <span class="kw">MODIFY</span> salary <span class="kw">DECIMAL</span>(12,2);

<span class="cm">-- Drop a column</span>
<span class="kw">ALTER TABLE</span> employees <span class="kw">DROP COLUMN</span> email;</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 6 : DROP -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DDL Command 3 — DROP</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">DROP</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Permanently deletes a table (or other object) along with <b>all of its data and structure</b>. This action cannot be rolled back — use with caution!</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Remove the employees table completely</span>
<span class="kw">DROP TABLE</span> employees;</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 7 : TRUNCATE -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DDL Command 4 — TRUNCATE</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">TRUNCATE</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Removes <b>all rows</b> from a table instantly, but keeps the table structure (columns, constraints) intact so new data can be inserted later. Faster than DELETE for removing everything.</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Delete all rows, keep the table structure</span>
<span class="kw">TRUNCATE TABLE</span> employees;</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 8 : DML Intro / INSERT -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DML Command 1 — INSERT</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">INSERT</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Adds one or more new rows of data into an existing table. You specify the table name, the columns, and the values to be stored.</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Insert a single row</span>
<span class="kw">INSERT INTO</span> employees (emp_id, first_name, last_name, salary)
<span class="kw">VALUES</span> (1, <span class="str">'Prince'</span>, <span class="str">'Kumar'</span>, 75000.00);

<span class="cm">-- Insert multiple rows at once</span>
<span class="kw">INSERT INTO</span> employees (emp_id, first_name, salary)
<span class="kw">VALUES</span> (2, <span class="str">'Anita'</span>, 62000.00),
       (3, <span class="str">'Ravi'</span>, 58000.00);</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 9 : UPDATE -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DML Command 2 — UPDATE</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">UPDATE</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Modifies the values of existing rows. Always use a <b>WHERE clause</b> to target specific rows — without it, every row in the table will be updated!</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Give Prince a salary raise</span>
<span class="kw">UPDATE</span> employees
<span class="kw">SET</span> salary = 85000.00
<span class="kw">WHERE</span> emp_id = 1;

<span class="cm">-- Update every employee's salary (no WHERE)</span>
<span class="kw">UPDATE</span> employees <span class="kw">SET</span> salary = salary * 1.10;</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 10 : DELETE -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>DML Command 3 — DELETE</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <span class="cmd">DELETE</span>
    <p><b>Purpose:</b> Removes one or more rows from a table based on a condition. Like UPDATE, the WHERE clause is critical — omitting it deletes <b>all rows</b> (but keeps the table structure).</p>
  </div>
  <pre><span class="cm">-- Delete one specific employee</span>
<span class="kw">DELETE FROM</span> employees
<span class="kw">WHERE</span> emp_id = 3;

<span class="cm">-- Delete all rows (table remains)</span>
<span class="kw">DELETE FROM</span> employees;</pre>
</div>

<!-- SLIDE 11 : Summary -->
<div class="slide">
  <h2>Summary — All 7 Commands</h2>
  <table class="summary-table">
    <tr><th>Command</th><th>Type</th><th>What it does</th></tr>
    <tr><td>CREATE</td><td>DDL</td><td>Creates a new table / object</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ALTER</td><td>DDL</td><td>Modifies table structure</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DROP</td><td>DDL</td><td>Deletes table + data permanently</td></tr>
    <tr><td>TRUNCATE</td><td>DDL</td><td>Removes all rows, keeps structure</td></tr>
    <tr><td>INSERT</td><td>DML</td><td>Adds new rows of data</td></tr>
    <tr><td>UPDATE</td><td>DML</td><td>Changes existing rows</td></tr>
    <tr><td>DELETE</td><td>DML</td><td>Removes rows of data</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

